    "statementMarkdown": "The $2m$ numbers\n\n$$\n1\\cdot2,\\ 2\\cdot3,\\ 3\\cdot4,\\ \\ldots,\\ 2m(2m+1)\n$$\n\nare written on a blackboard, where $m\\ge2$ is an integer. A move consists of choosing three numbers $a,b,c$, erasing them from the board and writing the single number\n\n$$\n\\frac{abc}{ab+bc+ca}.\n$$\n\nAfter $m-1$ such moves, only two numbers will remain on the blackboard. Supposing one of these is $\\frac43$, show that the other is larger than 4.\n",
